Summary: Compile with -fPIC, not -fpic
Keywords: 


The dynamic loader resolves the GOT entries when the program starts (the
dynamic loader is not part of GCC; it is part of the operating system).
If the GOT size for the linked executable exceeds a machine-specific
maximum size, you get an error message from the linker indicating that
`-fpic' does not work; in that case, recompile with `-fPIC' instead.
(These maximums are 8k on the SPARC and 32k on the m68k and RS/6000.  The
386 has no such limit.) Hit the limit on sparc.

* src/Makefile (%.lo): compile with -fPIC, not -fpic
(%.o): Ditto

